      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-81766",
        "knowledge_point_id": "67e90c94-5018-582f-8692-a1155f41f7c7",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding Differences of Sets Given Verbally",
        "problem": "Let $A$  be the set of all multiples of $3$ greater than $0$ and let $B$  be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0.$ What is $B-A?$",
        "worked_solution": "The multiples of $3$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B-A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $12,24,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-A & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}-{3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "{3,6,9,15,18,21,…}",
                "option": "0",
                "source_option": "a"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "{12,24…}",
                "option": "1",
                "source_option": "b"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "{4,8,16,20,…}",
                "option": "2",
                "source_option": "c"
              },
